    "answer": "onigiri/rice-ball-(often-triangular,-sometimes-with-a-filling-and-wrapped-in-nori)",
    "mnemonic": "<ja>握り</ja> is a \"grip.\" When you add <ja>お</ja> it's elevated a bit. For some reason it becomes a <vocabulary>rice ball</vocabulary> (aka <vocabulary>onigiri</vocabulary>). To make a rice ball, you use your grip to make them into a ball shape, which is probably where it comes from.",
